body.p:
4. Very nearly related to patience is meekness;
Cf. No. 22, ‘Sermon on the Mount, II’, I.4 and n. if it be not rather a species of it. For may it not be defined, patience of injuries, particularly affronts, reproach, or unjust censure? This teaches not to return evil for evil, or railing for railing; but contrariwise, blessing. Our blessed Lord himself seems to place a peculiar value upon this temper. This he peculiarly calls us to ‘learn of him’, if we would ‘find rest for our souls’.
Cf. Matt. 11:29.
